messages:
Nina (Partners): Quick heads-up: were planning a partner-facing API envelope change. Move `meta` fields to top-level and rename header `X-Partner-Key` -> `X-Partner-Key-V2`. Target ~6-week runway. Need marketplace resubmission, hardware partner QA, and SI release notes. Who owns partner comms + migration helpers?

Carlos (SDK): Can you paste a minimal before/after? Also does this touch streaming frames or just sync responses?

Nina (Partners): Affects sync + streaming context frames. Minimal diff: 
```json
// old
{"meta":{"req_id":"r-123","region":"us-east-1"},"data":{...}}
// new
{"req_id":"r-123","region":"us-east-1","service_hint":"edge","data":{...}}
// header change: X-Partner-Key -> X-Partner-Key-V2
```

Rohit (Runtime): I can implement a runtime compatibility shim that rewrites v3 -> v2 and expose a per-tenant toggle. Will aim for a PR in ~2 weeks. Also add telemetry when shim used.

Maya (Ops): Ops asks for a canary + runbook. Suggest 0.5% -> 2% staged canary, validate auth failures, 4xxs, and P95 latency. Roll back if auth failures > 0.5% absolute or P95 increases > 50ms. I will own the runbook and alerting.

Carlos (SDK): SDK plan: auto-detect new envelope and normalize to legacy shape for older apps. Provide env var to force v2/v3 for testing. Target release client 3.2.0 in ~10 business days. Will include Node/Python/Go snippets. Example normalize snippet: 
```js
const resp = await client.call(...);
if (resp.req_id && !resp.meta) {
  resp.meta = { req_id: resp.req_id, region: resp.region };
}
```

MarketplaceBot: Marketplace earliest resubmission slot: 2026-07-28. Standard review ~3 business days. Include migration guide in submission.

Nina (Partners): I'll collect signoffs from Ionix, EdgeWorks, FastIntegrate, AccelSys and request an embargo via Legal. Proposed timeline: Week 0 outreach + embargo, Week 2 internal canary, Week 4 partner QA, Week 6 public + marketplace resubmit. Owners: SDK=Carlos, Runtime=Rohit, Ops=Maya, Outreach=Nina.

Carlos (SDK): No objections. I'll add migration examples and telemetry hooks.

Rohit (Runtime): Will add console toggle and a 90-day compatibility mode for tenants that need more runway.

Maya (Ops): I'll share the canary runbook and alert thresholds by EOD.

Nina (Partners): Thanks all  kicking off outreach this afternoon. Please drop PR/trackers in the shared doc when you have them.
